Package: os7-desktop
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: metapackages
Priority: important
Depends: os7-base (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-backup (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-desktop-theme (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-app-softwareupdate (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Conflicts: os7-server
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 — the GUI product
 What a machine installed in GUI mode is: everything os7-server has, plus OS/7
 Classic, the Windows 2000 surface for GNOME, and OS/7's own graphical
 applications.
 .
 The applications are members here rather than in os7-base because a headless
 machine has nothing to draw them on: the headless path purges the desktop and
 then runs `apt-get autoremove -y --purge`, and membership is what lets that
 take them with it.
 .
 x86_64 only, and that is a Microsoft constraint rather than an OS/7 preference:
 Edge, the Intune portal and the identity broker have no arm64 builds, and
 Intune enrollment requires a GNOME desktop. The package is Architecture: all
 because its own content is architecture-independent; what makes it amd64-only
 is that its dependencies do not resolve anywhere else.
 .
 Conflicts with os7-server, because the two are the setup-time choice and not a
 runtime toggle.
